Engineering Statics — Baker and Haynes (@mech-statics-book: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mech-sources) { r_3DXGKGQSPPA9YDNH2WSB8XRN80
Daniel W. Baker and William Haynes. Engineering Statics: Open and Interactive. [Author site](https://engineeringstatics.org/) · [Complete PDF](https://engineeringstatics.org/pdf/statics.pdf) · [Source repository](https://github.com/dantheboatman/EngineeringStatics).

The inspected PDF is dated 26 September 2026. Its cover, licence, contents and selected statics passages were inspected on 30 October 2026; a temporary reading copy was retained outside the repository. The ten chapters proceed from basic quantities and vectors through equilibrium, moments, structures, centroids, internal actions, friction and geometric inertia. Work the whole text and exercises progressively.

Text is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0; GeoGebra components are identified as CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 with additional component notices. Keep attribution and the actual edition. The PDF gives a static reading version; interactive examples have their own online/software requirements. The book supplies a statics foundation, not a complete machine-design education.

**Return:** [Mechanical-engineering sources](../Sources.lingua#r_06RZYPZEFNMZ6MZ690QB1WN1Z2).

**Second physics-block inspection — 31 October 2026:** the current author-hosted web text and chapter-4/5 contents were inspected, with selected passages in [4.1, moments](https://engineeringstatics.org/moment-of-force.html), [4.5, couples](https://engineeringstatics.org/Chapter_04-couples.html), [4.7, equivalent systems](https://engineeringstatics.org/statically-equivalent-systems.html), [5.2, free-body diagrams](https://engineeringstatics.org/Chapter_05-free-body-diagrams.html), [5.3, equilibrium equations](https://engineeringstatics.org/Chapter_05-equations-of-equilibrium.html), and [5.6, stability/determinacy](https://engineeringstatics.org/Chapter_05-stability-and-determinacy.html). The block assigns selected planar work from 4.1–4.3, 4.5–4.7, 5.1–5.4 and 5.6. This assignment is broader than the inspected passages; no complete exercise or interactive-media audit is claimed. Interpret the source's stability criteria within its idealized restraints: the new explanation separately treats unilateral contact, redundant reactions and later load-dependent stability. Original fixture and finite uniform-load examples are separate from the textbook examples. The existing complete-text assignment and component rights notices remain applicable.

